<body>
    <h1>Current User Management - Known issues &amp; gaps</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p>This page summarizes the known issues and gaps found in current user=
 management features. The root cause, workaround and Jira ticket reference =
will be mentioned, if applicable.</p>
    <p>
     <style type=3D"text/css">/*<![CDATA[*/
div.rbtoc1788185664955 {padding: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1788185664955 ul {margin-left: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1788185664955 li {margin-left: 0px;padding-left: 0px;}

/*]]>*/</style></p>
    <div class=3D"toc-macro rbtoc1788185664955">
     <ul class=3D"toc-indentation">
      <li><a href=3D"#CurrentUserManagementKnownissues&amp;gaps-ManageUserL=
ist">Manage User List</a></li>
      <li><a href=3D"#CurrentUserManagementKnownissues&amp;gaps-Create/Upda=
teUserDetails">Create / Update User Details</a></li>
      <li><a href=3D"#CurrentUserManagementKnownissues&amp;gaps-UserExtract=
andBulkUserUpdate">User Extract and Bulk User Update</a></li>
     </ul>
    </div>
    <p></p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h2 id=3D"CurrentUserManagementKnownissues&amp;gaps-ManageUserList">Man=
age User List</h2>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper=
 confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image i=
mage-center" draggable=3D"false" height=3D"277" src=3D"3936a8529d4090b77001=
5423889c05bc54f6b59f0a8d57f593663151cf0c8d89" data-image-src=3D"/download/a=
ttachments/2774376605/image-2026-6-25_18-13-18.png?version=3D1&amp;modifica=
tionDate=3D1782425598787&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" =
data-linked-resource-id=3D"2774398120" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" d=
ata-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=
=3D"image-2026-6-25_18-13-18.png" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" dat=
a-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container=
-id=3D"2774376605" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"9" tabindex=3D=
"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></span></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><span>1. User Status</span></p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"c0a2837b-d5fd-46c0-8986-6d9c090170d4">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: User status is not updated correctly in some situations, for instance, =
when a user locks themselves out after too many failed login attempts.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"2212ea52-b44c-439e-a2a4-c46325743605">Root cause: Use=
r status is not synced up from IDP (Okta) in a reasonable time for the user=
 login activities via Okta widget or Client IDP SSO.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"66c7b2ac-541b-433f-bd51-9bfa7bb03905">Business/Operat=
ion impact: Medium</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"c9562c29-65c7-426a-a5b8-8546c9bc3053"><span>Workaroun=
ds: Run a forced "data pull" from Okta on the record, wait for the next dat=
a cache to happen, execute a user status sync in backend.</span></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ba0715c3-0b46-438d-b37d-49bee26cbf51">Jira ticket: Av=
ailable in the backlog. High-level solution direction is to implement Event=
 Sourcing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>2. Create User</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"7c619daf-9d26-49bf-bab6-cf3a3c3d9c68">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: ID administrators sometimes create new user accounts in the wrong firm =
as they forget to select the correct firm first.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"88382e2b-8543-4d3f-a977-f98de38c67e0">Root cause: The=
 product concept that a user account is associated to one and only one firm=
, and the product design assuming administrators are mindful in selecting t=
he correct firm first</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"2265cfa7-873c-437b-9d94-e296d61a3738">Business/Operat=
ion impact: Medium</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"eebf6ab6-3f6b-4fc1-a02d-c8214d3c8ac3">Workarounds: Th=
e user account created in the wrong firm cannot be switched to the correct =
firm; instead, it will often be abandoned (deactivated) and a new user acco=
unt will be created for the client, however, the user id will be padded wit=
h a digit, e.g. john.doe1, which is not neat.&nbsp;</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"59f8deb1-eaa4-4a42-b3f6-04f7ff51f726">Jira ticket: Av=
ailable in the backlog. High-level solution direction is to provide a firm-=
switching feature for firm context correction.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">3. Features access provisions=
 based on selected firm-scope&nbsp;</span></p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"9c276dc4-2e5d-45e1-828b-08377cfbd406">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: The access provisions of the "Export" and "Upload" features are tied to=
 the selected firm scope. For instance, if the user admin has selected "NBI=
N" firm, then the full capabilities of the features will be available; howe=
ver, if a client firm is selected, then only limited capabilities of the fe=
atures will be available. It is the same user but the access provisions wil=
l be differed based on the selected firm-scope.=20
      <ul>
       <li>The intention is to enable a smooth transition to client firm se=
lf-serve user management, however, it is confusing to some user admin perso=
nnel.</li>
       <li>The current implementation is to hard-coded it, which is hard to=
 scale and maintain.</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"8bb4cd83-107f-4c13-a9ef-45ab1e82c074">Root cause: It =
is a unique access control design as it does not align to the firm package =
concept.&nbsp;</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"b94e695e-5524-4be3-b541-e6283b4d1697">Workarounds: Th=
ere is no workarounds.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"b69e547e-77be-4d02-b3c3-e165838dd013">Jira ticket: No=
t available.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>4. User search by role</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"bd0a1827-3c67-456d-a618-7496e5bc58eb">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: User search by the role description (e.g. "Manage All") does not work b=
ecause the search looks up the technical role names, e.g. ManageAll - witho=
ut a space. However, due to typos or shortened names, the tech role names a=
re not always straightforward. For example, the tech role name for "Manage =
Firm and User" is MangeFirm&nbsp;=20
      <ul>
       <li>It disables Product team to search users by role quickly</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"3d720c88-d68c-45f4-926c-13aab9ba69fb">Root cause: The=
 solution does not support user search by role description, which is resolv=
ed via Content API, not from backend call directly.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"591e6f3c-634a-4895-907e-c2e4c9db3d33">Workarounds: Th=
ere is no workarounds.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"489f393a-c172-4e8a-a9eb-9330f3780015">Jira ticket: Av=
ailable in the backlog.</li>
    </ul>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h2 id=3D"CurrentUserManagementKnownissues&amp;gaps-Create/UpdateUserDe=
tails">Create / Update User Details</h2>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper=
 confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image i=
mage-center" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"468" src=3D"8de4bab318f4c23e0aa42=
813acaf6e65f855323da12eedcdf68d13643099a91d" data-image-src=3D"/download/at=
tachments/2774376605/image-2026-6-26_9-51-47.png?version=3D1&amp;modificati=
onDate=3D1782481907403&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" da=
ta-linked-resource-id=3D"2774400533" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" dat=
a-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D=
"image-2026-6-26_9-51-47.png" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-li=
nked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=
=3D"2774376605" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"9" tabindex=3D"0"=
 alt=3D"" height=3D"541"></span></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p>1. Module list&nbsp;</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"001809f5-58c9-4ace-86ba-f52fcd7093e8">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: The module list contains all modules available for visibility restricti=
on (show/hide) on the selected role. The list has grown and becoming out-of=
-control.&nbsp;=20
      <ul>
       <li>The modules are not listed in alphabetical order nor grouped by =
product group, making it hard to go through and locate the module you are l=
ooking for.</li>
       <li>The list does not remove modules which have been opted out by th=
e user's firm, causing redundance.</li>
       <li>When creating a new user, all modules are selected by default (c=
hecked), however, a repeating user feedback is to set them all as unselecte=
d by default.</li>
       <li>The solution does not handle dependencies among modules. For ins=
tance, the client document modules (Statements, Tax Documents, Trade Confir=
mations) must not be selected without Account modules, otherwise, they cann=
ot be navigated to.</li>
       <li>It does not prevent user admin to unselect ALL modules, which sh=
ould be flagged as an error.</li>
       <li>It also does not prevent user admin to only select modules which=
 are not integrated in Compass, e.g. external apps. For instance, if the on=
ly selected modules are Compass (Legacy), Tools, Onboarding: Paper Upload o=
r Onboarding: Form Applications, the user cannot use Compass properly.</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"261b7ec4-b7ae-44da-8a99-ee99bcd932bb">Root cause: The=
re are technical difficulties due to the complexity of the restriction reso=
urce, heavy-loaded business logics to "customize" visibility on more granul=
ar level and the challenges of feature package updates.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"430078ee-1f46-402a-a4c4-f85892c74753">Workarounds: Th=
ere is no workarounds.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"f7abeef4-36ac-42df-94ad-865c3be3e4bc">Jira ticket: No=
t available.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">2. Additional features&nbsp;<=
/span></p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"dafbec8e-60ba-4c38-8fdf-ee984641bb5d">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: Additional features are the options to enrich or advance user's access =
provision in the specified module, however, it is often mixed up.=20
      <ul>
       <li>The additional features are sometimes selected but the module th=
ey operate in is not. For instance, when the "Manage Equity Orders" feature=
 is selected but the "Orders" module is not selected, the user cannot acces=
s any order entry feature.</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"74c10bea-68eb-4ed5-81f9-ea6391ffdd09">The additiona=
l features are sometimes redundant. For instance, as the "view" access is t=
he default page associated to the module, it is not necessary to set up a "=
view" feature as an additional feature.</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"a5a8990a-ac70-43a3-81e0-19542ded6556">Root cause: Lac=
k of the visual linkage of the modules and their additional features on use=
r admin tool.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"cd972169-f1ba-40b6-8483-67ba718a1802">Workarounds: Th=
ere is no workarounds.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"11dccf65-06f6-4c8a-ad99-baa4a393d2f9">Jira ticket: No=
t available.</li>
    </ul>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h2 id=3D"CurrentUserManagementKnownissues&amp;gaps-UserExtractandBulkU=
serUpdate"><span>User Extract and Bulk User Update</span></h2>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper=
 confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image i=
mage-center" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"468" src=3D"7f3d8c741b09ac8af385f=
b601afe5b59557cfbc0989d1242a8959edcbe96118a" data-image-src=3D"/download/at=
tachments/2774376605/image-2026-6-26_16-8-38.png?version=3D1&amp;modificati=
onDate=3D1782504518552&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" da=
ta-linked-resource-id=3D"2778829308" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" dat=
a-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D=
"image-2026-6-26_16-8-38.png" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-li=
nked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=
=3D"2774376605" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"9" tabindex=3D"0"=
 alt=3D"" height=3D"217"></span></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper=
 confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image i=
mage-center" draggable=3D"false" width=3D"468" src=3D"2f620eb7989cb12458239=
a77fe0a5891cf3688d27a50d1098469218ca0f780a7" data-image-src=3D"/download/at=
tachments/2774376605/image-2026-6-26_16-9-21.png?version=3D1&amp;modificati=
onDate=3D1782504561974&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" da=
ta-linked-resource-id=3D"2778829316" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" dat=
a-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D=
"image-2026-6-26_16-9-21.png" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-li=
nked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=
=3D"2774376605" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"9" tabindex=3D"0"=
 alt=3D"" height=3D"84"></span></p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p>High-level workflow: Use the Users: Exports tool to generate a CSV f=
ile, modify the data values of selected user accounts, then use the Users: =
Uploads tool to upload the revised file to bulk update user accounts.</p>
    <p>There are several issues &amp; gaps with the system-generated CSV fi=
le.</p>
    <p>1. Role column, Default Module column, Features column</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"8130711e-186f-4cfb-b401-0e7cd0ba98c1"><span>Issues &a=
mp; gaps: The technical names&nbsp;for these columns are produced in the ex=
tract file and are expected by the bulk user update tool, which is</span> n=
ot user-friendly.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"3e044ff2-c5d8-4fdf-b7f0-525ef4632233">Root cause: Usa=
bility is compromised in the solution.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"d2d70ad5-120e-4661-aeed-a4ae91d138d8">Workarounds: Th=
ere is no workarounds; Product users will have to keep a reference sheet fo=
r all tech names.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"8ccef568-e660-4a9f-9a3f-eb5dc7aea1d9">Jira ticket: No=
t available.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>2. RR Code Assignment</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ab09c818-7f0a-4a42-bb24-a844ce72312a">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: The RR code assignments must be coded as a range with a dash between th=
e from value and the to value, even for a single RR code, which is counter-=
intuitive.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"98ad068f-d377-4f25-b7fd-1e58f0dfb296">Root cause: Usa=
bility is compromised in the solution.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"0b2bece5-6b32-4e9e-9cd6-960b3c775347">Workarounds: Th=
ere is no workarounds.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"8191822b-8905-41ee-9130-2209f584deb1">Jira ticket: No=
t available.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">3. Module Overrides column</s=
pan></p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"f4c34d09-8879-4f98-a39d-55113d2ee3b4">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: It lists the modules having the restriction resource selected (i.e. wha=
t are "unchecked" on the UI), causing a challenge for those who consume the=
 user extract for user analysis and those who modify the data files for bul=
k user role updates.=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"be906731-3b4b-4ce7-b520-56c5b1728445">Product users=
 is unable to screen the eligible modules for users from the list - the lis=
t shows what modules they are <u>not</u> assigned to only.</li>
       <li>When they want to bulk update users, instead of specifying what =
modules the user should be assigned to, the Product user will have to list =
the opposites, which is both counter-intuitive and error-prone.</li>
       <li>As the default of module selection is selected (i.e. "checked"),=
 in case the Product user misses any modules which are provisioned in the s=
elected user package but not eligible to the user, the module will be assig=
ned to the user anyway, which is why updating this column is very risky.</l=
i>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"d6500fdc-cdd7-4a40-b7b0-d9c4cb7be390">Root cause: Usa=
bility is compromised in the solution and the complexity of the restriction=
 resource making it worse.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"6bbfaf59-9b7b-4da9-9c4a-ab66a1e1f4fa">Workarounds: Th=
ere is no workarounds.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"c6c8eec5-bc53-4faf-a720-7bd51146a777">Jira ticket: No=
t available.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>4. Field edits (validation)</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"49260074-cffb-4529-aa92-a430122144fe">Issues &amp; ga=
ps: The field edits applied in the bulk user update process and those appli=
ed in the single user update (via UI) are sourced differently, causing inco=
nsistencies and scalability concern.=20
      <ul>
       <li>Though&nbsp;there is no known discrepancy between the two sets o=
f edits as of now, the error messages appear on the UI are different from t=
hose returned in the bulk user update process, in which they are less well-=
versed and more confusing to Product users.&nbsp;</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"b731becd-9214-4675-a74a-45bb513b3ef7">Due to the du=
plication, dev &amp; qa efforts are doubled whenever there is a change to t=
he user update edits, increasing the cost and vulnerability of the solution=
.</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"fdb0cacf-ffc2-4ca7-866c-4645f0c3433a">Root cause: Mis=
sed in detailed solution design, compromised to time-to-market need (for a =
quick turnaround).</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"793ba7ae-45ca-4c5f-82d4-52106be98787">Workarounds: Th=
ere is no workarounds.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ce70c72c-6792-4ed0-8db7-91b7534c2ad4">Jira ticket: No=
t available. High-level solution direction is to create a common lib for bo=
th front-end and back-end to source field edits.&nbsp;</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
